        {
          "id": 459460353,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The current approach is the same as what is used for parsing other TLVs across DOCSIS dissection routines. It comes from the nature of the DOCSIS MAC management packets payload: we don't know the length of a TLV until we get to the Length field (which comes after Type). Hence, proto_item_set_len() is used once we know the length of the payload. I haven't seen anyone setting the length of a TLV to -1 before calling proto_item_set_len() for DOCSIS.\n\nUnless the current approach introduces new risk(s), I would prefer to leave it as is, for the sake of consistency. The dissection works correctly when I unit-test it on a sample PCAP.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7405680,
            "username": "tulup1",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Andrii Vladyka",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
